---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

// STARTER_CONTENT: replace the hero artwork and its alt text below, then
// remove this comment.
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A lecture theatre reduced to flat gold and black shapes, rows of seats sweeping past the frame, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Seven studios hand you a small provocation and turn you loose on it with
    the rest of the room — overanalysing a text message in layers, guessing
    the ending of something a classmate overthought, making and eating a
    sandwich in complete silence, running the same excessive rigour on a
    best-case scenario instead of a worst one. Three lectures, held outdoors,
    supply the actual research behind it. Every class opens with ten minutes
    of nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>What it isn't</h2>
  <p>
    Not a wellness course, and not therapy. The science here is real and
    cited, including the parts where the evidence is thinner than the internet
    suggests — you will be told which claims are findings and which are
    someone's hunch. It also takes almost nothing seriously, which turns out
    to be the point rather than a tone choice.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has re-read a two-word reply more times than it deserved, or
    shelved a decision because thinking about it further felt like progress.
    No background in psychology or philosophy assumed — the only prerequisite
    is a mind willing to catch itself in the act. Nothing you share is marked,
    and you can pass on any activity without giving a reason.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>What happens in each studio, and what to bring.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>The three outdoor lectures, and the research behind them.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
